THOUGHT: The logs confirm persistent write locks across nodes, while the current design has no process-wide serialization for SQLite writes. I’ll add an external `flock`-based transaction lock around the request handler’s write operations by wrapping SQLite connections with a lock acquired only when a transaction begins; this prevents concurrent node writers from leaving incompatible WAL transactions and allows clean commits.

```mswea_bash_command
